Data credits. The license covers our code. It does not cover NASA's data.

- The positions of the Sun and the Earth come from NASA JPL Horizons
  (https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/api/horizons.api). The file
  planner/data/ephemeris.bin is made from that output.
- The horizons come from the LRO LOLA south-pole elevation model
  (Barker et al. 2023, Planetary Science Journal 4, 183,
  doi:10.3847/PSJ/acf3e1), from NASA PGDA. The elevation model is not in
  this repository.
- Check V3 reads a small number of values from the LOLA average illumination
  map AVGVISIB_85S_060M_201608 (Mazarico et al. 2011, Icarus 211, 1066-1081,
  doi:10.1016/j.icarus.2010.10.030).
- Names and positions of lunar features: IAU Gazetteer of Planetary
  Nomenclature (USGS). Apollo landing sites: NASA NSSDC.

We did not confirm the terms of use of Horizons output and of the PGDA
products. Confirm them, and correct this file if they need other words.

